  "body": "## Overview\n\nThis PR skips automatic RAM prompt-cache saves and prompt-reuse checkpoints for `cache_prompt = false` tasks. It avoids checkpoint copies and extra ubatches on recurrent, hybrid, and SWA models, and skips automatic cache saves on other models too. Both LRU and idle-slot saves respect the task's caching policy. Requests with `cache_prompt = true`, live-prefix reuse, and explicit slot saves remain supported; explicitly restored state becomes cacheable again.\n\n## Benchmark Summary\n\n- AMD Radeon PRO W7800 48 GB, `gfx1100` / RDNA3; Vulkan, RADV / Mesa `26.0.8-1ubuntu0.3`\n- Qwen3.8 27B Q8_0 hybrid + MTP Q4_0 draft\n- `--ctx-size 32768 --cache-ram 20480 -b 2048 -ub 2048 --parallel 1`\n- `-ctk f16 -ctv f16 --flash-attn on --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 3`\n- Upstream `c811cb8f0` versus final revision `96e1d229f`, including the restore fix; `A-B-B-A`\n- Per binary: 60 no-cache probes (13 tokens, `n_predict = 1`) and 12 following cache-enabled requests with unique 1.4\u20131.9k-token prompts; no cache hits\n\n| Measurement | Baseline | Candidate |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Probe prompt time, p50 | 269.5 ms | 107.7 ms (-60.0%) |\n| Following request: slot selection to launch, median | 156.6 ms | 0.03 ms |\n| Following request: wall time, median | 2718.0 ms | 2566.1 ms |\n\nSelection-to-launch captures the avoided cache save. Following-request prompt evaluation was similar: 2557.8 \u2192 2562.5 ms.\n\n**Testing:** all 21 CPU cases in `test_kv_keep_only_active.py` and `test_slot_save.py` pass. `test_nocache_prompt_not_saved` fails on master; the restore regression fails without its fix. Both pass on this branch.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Yes, I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- AI usage disclosure: YES, AI was used for implementation, tests, benchmarks, review. I reviewed the final diff and can explain all code changes.",
